  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Hirsutene and the CD70 antigen, as all three paths point to Hirsutene acting as a target of a compound (Gentirigeoside E, Cassiaoccidentalin B, or Pinoresinol-4-O-Beta-Monoglycoside) that ultimately targets the CD70 antigen. The high scores in all three paths (final_score=0.6248) indicate a consistent and robust relationship, with Hirsutene serving as a central node in the pathway leading to CD70. The shared target of these compounds in LoVo cells suggests a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of cellular signaling pathways that regulate CD70 expression. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Hirsutene may influence CD70 through the activation or inhibition of downstream targets in LoVo cells. The evidence is consistent and does not require additional layers of complexity, making it a compelling candidate for a direct relationship between Hirsutene and CD70.",
